title:: BMAbstractAudioChainElement
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - abstract superclass of audio chain elements
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMAbstractAudioChainElement is the abstract superclass of all BEASTmulch Library objects which serve as elements in an audio chain. This includes sources (subclasses of link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioSource::), such as link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayer::, routers and mixers such as link::Classes/Matrices/BMAudioMatrix:: and link::Classes/Matrices/BMAmpControlMatrix::, and processors and spatialisers such as link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsRack:: and link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRack::. As such it defines a standard interface and a number of inherited methods.

Subclasses generally create a link::Classes/Group:: to hold all of their nodes which is stored in the group instance variable.

For the sake of simplicity and to avoid conflicts subclasses of BMAbstractAudioChain do no rebuilding on Cmd-. If you want to do this simply add a link::Classes/Function:: to rebuild the chain to link::Classes/ServerTree::.

You can see a list of all available subclasses by executing the following:

code::
BMAbstractAudioChainElement.dumpClassSubtree;
::

See also: link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractMatrix::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioSource::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractController::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::

Section:: Making chains of elements

Subclasses take instances of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: to specify input and/or busses. In some cases output busses will be the same as inputs, in others (notably link::Classes/Matrices/BMAudioMatrix::) take separate outputs. strong::*new:: methods generally call strong::asBMInOutArray:: on strong::ins:: and strong::outs::, which most subclasses implement to return their output array. This means that instances can be passed as arguments for these. Some classes (e.g. subclasses of link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioSource::) do not take inputs and supply their outputs as a private bus.

strong::asTarget:: is implemented to return the object's strong::group::, which means that you can pass audio chain elements most places you would pass a link::Classes/Node::, e.g. as a target for a link::Classes/Synth::.

By convention subclasses of link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioSource:: use code::\addToHead:: as their default strong::addAction::, and all other subclasses of BMAbstractAudioChainElement use code::\addToTail::. This means that in most cases chains of objects can be created in the order they will appear on the server.

The examples below demonstrate this.

CLASSMETHODS::
	
method:: allChainElements
An link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: containing all active instances of this class' subclasses. This can be used to query the library to see which chain elements exist at the moment.
		
INSTANCEMETHODS::
		
method:: addAction
Returns this object's strong::addAction::, which determines where its strong::group:: will be created relative to its strong::target::. See subclasses for details.
				
method:: target
Returns this object's strong::target::, which determines the relative position at which its strong::group:: will be created base on its strong::addAction:: See subclasses for details.
				
method::ins
Returns this object's inputs as a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::.
				
