INSTANCEMETHODS::

The following methods specify the minimum interface for a BMAbstractAudioChainElement; some notes about subclassing are included. In some cases the methods simply return a SubclassResponsibilityError, and should be overridden in subclasses.

Implementations of strong::*new:: in subclasses should take at least strong::target::, strong::addAction::, and strong::name:: as arguments.

code::
// simplest case
*new { |outs, target, addAction = \addToTail, name| 
	^super.new.initNameAndTarget(target, addAction, name);
}
::
	
Subclasses which take strong::ins:: or strong::outs:: as arguments to *new should implement an init method to copy those to the corresponding instance vars, and fill in strong::inNames:: and strong::outNames::.

code::
// example with ins and outs
*new { |ins, outs, target, addAction = \addToTail, name|
	^super.new.init(ins.asBMInOutArray, outs.asBMInOutArray, target, addAction, name);
}
	
init {|argins, argouts, argTarget, argAddAction, argName|
	this.initNameAndTarget(argTarget, argAddAction, argName);
	ins = argins;
	outs = argouts;
	inNames = ins.keys;
	outNames = outs.keys;
}
::
	
	
	
method:: initNameAndTarget	
Converts strong::argtarget:: to a valid target, calls strong::makeName:: if needed, and adds this object to strong::allChainElements::. Subclasses should call this method from their strong::*new:: or strong::init:: methods. 
	
argument:: argtarget
Target for this object's Group. If target is not a link::Classes/Group:: or link::Classes/Synth::, it will be converted as follows: If it is a link::Classes/Server::, it will be converted to the default_group of that server. If it is nil, to the default_group of the default Server. strong::Note::: A Synth is not a valid target for code::\addToHead:: and strong::\addToTail::.

argument:: argaddAction
one of the following Symbols:		
code::\addToHead:: - (the default for BMAbstractAudioSources) add at the head of the group specified by strong::target::
code::\addToTail:: - (the default for most subclasses) add at the tail of the group specified by strong::target::
code::\addAfter:: - add immediately after strong::target:: in its server's node order
code::\addBefore:: - add immediately before strong::target:: in its server's node order
code::\addReplace:: - replace strong::target:: and take its place in its server's node order

argument:: argname
Explanation of argname. Default value is nil. Other information.

code::
// simplest case
initNameAndTarget {|argtarget, argaddAction, argname|
	target = argtarget.asTarget;
	server = target.server;
	addAction = argaddAction;
	name = (argname ?? {this.makeName}).asSymbol;
	allChainElements[name] = this;
	this.makeGroup;
}
::

method:: gui
This should create and return an appropriate GUI, usually using a specific GUI class (e.g. link::Classes/Matrices/BMMatrixGUI:: for matrices) with this as an argument.


method:: mappings
This methods should be implemented to allow getting or setting presets, i.e. they should set or get the global state of the object. Usually these return or take some sort of link::Classes/IdentityDictionary::. The default implementations do nothing.


method:: makeGroup
Makes this object's link::Classes/Group:: using strong::target:: and strong::addAction::.


method:: makeName
Automatically generate a strong::name:: for this object if one has not been supplied.


method:: free
The default implementation frees strong::group:: and removes this object from strong::allChainElements::. Subclasses should override this to do any necessary cleanup of resources. Once called, objects should not be used again.


method:: asTarget
Returns the element's link::Classes/Group::. This means that chain elements can be passed directly as targets in most cases. Subclasses can override this to return something else if appropriate.
		


Examples

// making an audio chain

s.boot;

// make a 5.1 speaker list (-0.1) for outputs
(
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

// make a controller
c = BMVirtualController.new('Level Sliders', s, 4); // new controller
g = BMVirtualControllerSliders(c); // GUI sliders for it

//// sources
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(8, name:\foo); // maximum 8 channel soundfile player
p.read("sounds/a11wlk01.wav"); // mono, so only out foo-1
p.gui;

b = Bus.audio(s, 1);
x = {Out.ar(b, PinkNoise.ar(0.2))}.play(target: p, addAction:\addAfter); // a noise source; note p works as a target

// do some processing at this stage
t = BMTrimPluginsRack(p.asBMInOutArray ++ b.asBMInOutArray(\noiseBus), x, \addAfter); // x as target
t.gui;

// make a matrix for connections
m = BMAudioMatrix(t, l, name:'Router'); 

// a matrix to map controls to scale amplitude
a = BMAmpControlMatrix(c, l, name:'Level Control'); // ins are the controller's control busses

m.gui; a.gui; // make some assignments here

// congrats, you've now got sources->trim-plugins->routing->level-scaling->outputs
// turn up your controllers to listen

[p, c, b, x, m, a, t].do(_.free); // cleanup
